<title>JAPAN: Eisai's Alzheimer's drug approved by 12 countries.</title>
<headline>Eisai's Alzheimer's drug approved by 12 countries.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eisai Co Ltd said on Wednesday that 12 European countries had approved its drug for Alzheimer's disease and that it expected to receive marketing authorisation from the countries in the near future.</p>
<p>The approval was issued by drug authorities in Germany, France, Italy, Austria, Belgium, Luxembourg, Denmark, Finland, Greece, Ireland, Portugal and Sweden.</p>
<p>The company has been marketing the drug, Aricept, in the United States since January 1997, Eisai said in a statement. The drug received marketing authorisation in Britain in February.</p>
<p>The drug, to treat mild to moderate stages of Alzheimer's disease, is jointly marketed in the United States and Britain with Pfizer Inc, the statement said.</p>
</text>
